+// Simplified-Chinese localization for the TEESimulator WebUI (Integrity Fusion).
+//
+// Design: EVERY piece of UI text in this app funnels through dom.js's el() — either
+// the {text} attr, a string child, or a title/placeholder/aria-label attr. i18n.js
+// exports one function, t(s), that maps an English source string to Chinese:
+//   1. exact match in DICT
+//   2. first matching rule in RULES (for strings composed at runtime, e.g. "3 apps")
+//   3. otherwise the original string, unchanged
+//
+// This keeps the localization OUT of the views: no view file is modified for
+// translation, so upstream changes to views never conflict with this file. Strings
+// upstream renames silently fall back to English instead of breaking the render.
+//
+// Deliberately NOT translated: config tokens (patch / generation / system_property /
+// today / no), keymaster tag names (verifiedBootState, osPatchLevel, ...), security
+// level names (Software / TrustedEnvironment / StrongBox), package names, aliases,
+// log content, and anything a user would match against typed filter syntax
+// (class:generated etc.) — translating those would break matching or mislead.
+
+// ---- exact-match dictionary ---------------------------------------------
